Getting the source for the cytoscape-popper extension.

cytoscape-popper is a small adapter that positions a DOM element (such as a
tooltip) relative to a Cytoscape graph element. Cytoscape renders to a canvas,
so its nodes and edges have no DOM elements of their own; this extension
supplies a Popper-compatible reference that tracks an element's rendered
position.

The extension is "popper library agnostic": it bundles no Popper of its own and
is handed a factory at registration time. We wire it to the Popper v2
that RT already loads for Bootstrap, e.g.:

    cytoscape.use( cytoscapePopper( function (ref, content, opts) {
        return Popper.createPopper(ref, content, opts);
    } ) );

Version: 4.0.1

1. Obtain the release.

   NOTE: At the time of writing, the project's GitHub Releases page does not
   have a 4.0.1 release, even though the 4.0.1 commits are present in the
   repository. We therefore obtained the 4.0.1 build from the npm registry
   rather than from GitHub Releases:

       https://www.npmjs.com/package/cytoscape-popper
       https://unpkg.com/cytoscape-popper@4.0.1/cytoscape-popper.js
       https://unpkg.com/cytoscape-popper@4.0.1/LICENSE

2. The npm package contains a single prebuilt UMD bundle,
   cytoscape-popper.js (the global it defines is "cytoscapePopper"). There is
   nothing to build. Copy it in as the development source:

    cp cytoscape-popper.js ~/rt-dir/devel/third-party/cytoscape-popper/

3. The package ships no minified build, so generate the served minified copy
   ourselves. Use RT's own JS minifier (JavaScript::Minifier::XS, already an
   RT dependency) so no extra tooling is needed:

    perl -MJavaScript::Minifier::XS -e '
        local $/; open my $in, "<", "cytoscape-popper.js" or die $!;
        print JavaScript::Minifier::XS::minify(scalar <$in>);
    ' > ~/rt-dir/share/static/js/cytoscape-popper.min.js
